{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7c1e5b2a-3f4d-4e8a-9b6c-2d1f0a8e5c37",
    "name": "Hotel Availability Search",
    "description": "Endpoints de mindata-availability-search. La especificación OpenAPI está en openapi.yaml.\n\nOrden sugerido: ejecutar la carpeta \"Flujo feliz\" completa (Runner) — cada POST guarda su searchId en variables de colección y los GET /count esperan unos segundos porque la persistencia es asíncrona (REST -> Kafka -> Oracle).\n\nLa carpeta \"CORS\" simula el preflight que hace un browser (p. ej. \"Try it out\" de Swagger UI); {{corsOrigin}} debe estar en CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.\n\nRequisitos: docker compose up -d y la aplicación corriendo en {{baseUrl}}.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "corsOrigin",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081"
    },
    {
      "key": "hotelId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "searchId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "searchIdReordered",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "searchIdOtherAges",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "asyncWaitMs",
      "value": "2000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Flujo feliz",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /search",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// hotelId único por ejecución para que los conteos empiecen en cero.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('hotelId', 'hotel-' + pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$randomUUID}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('devuelve searchId', () => pm.expect(body.searchId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('searchId', body.searchId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"hotelId\": \"{{hotelId}}\",\n  \"checkIn\": \"29/12/2023\",\n  \"checkOut\": \"31/12/2023\",\n  \"ages\": [30, 29, 1, 3]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/search",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "search"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
